## Flutter Web Development with Live Reload

### Overview
Comprehensive Flutter web development commands optimized for live editing, hot reload, and debugging in the Plattr Pro Flutter Web App.

### Primary Development Commands

#### Quick Start (Recommended)
```bash
# 🚀 Quick start with logging (uses existing script)
./run_with_logs.sh

# 🌐 Standard development with consistent port
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer html

# 🔍 Debug mode with verbose logging
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --debug --verbose --web-renderer html
```

#### Alternative Development Commands
```bash
# 🧪 Chrome with isolated profile (testing)
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-browser-flag="--user-data-dir=/tmp/chrome_dev_test"

# ⚡ Hot reload with verbose output
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --verbose --web-renderer html

# 🎯 Auto web renderer selection
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer auto
```

### Development Workflow

#### Standard Development Flow
1. **Start the app**: `./run_with_logs.sh` or `flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080`
2. **Live editing**: Make changes to your Dart files
3. **Hot reload**: Press `r` in terminal or save files (auto-reload)
4. **Hot restart**: Press `R` for full app restart
5. **Quit**: Press `q` to stop development server

#### Advanced Development Flow
```bash
# 🔨 Complete development setup
flutter clean && \
flutter pub get && \
flutter packages pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs && \
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer html --debug
```

### Build Modes

#### Debug Mode (Default)
```bash
# 🐛 Full debug with DevTools
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --debug --web-renderer html
```

#### Profile Mode (Performance Testing)
```bash
# 🔧 Performance profiling
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --profile --web-renderer html
```

#### Release Mode (Production Testing)
```bash
# 🚀 Production-like testing
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --release --web-renderer html
```

### Environment-Specific Development

#### Development Environment
```bash
# 🔧 Development with full features
flutter run -d chrome \
  --web-port 8080 \
  --web-renderer html \
  --debug \
  --dart-define=ENV=development \
  --dart-define=API_DEBUG=true
```

#### Staging Environment
```bash
# 🧪 Staging environment testing
flutter run -d chrome \
  --web-port 8080 \
  --web-renderer html \
  --profile \
  --dart-define=ENV=staging
```

### Development Features

#### Hot Reload & Hot Restart
- **Hot Reload**: Instant UI changes without losing app state
- **Hot Restart**: Full app restart while maintaining development session
- **Chrome DevTools**: Full debugging with breakpoints, network inspection
- **Live Error Display**: Compilation errors shown directly in browser

#### Debugging Tools
```bash
# 🔍 Network debugging
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer html \
  --dart-define=API_DEBUG=true --dart-define=LOG_LEVEL=verbose

# 📊 Performance monitoring
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer html \
  --profile --trace-startup

# 🛠️ CORS testing (disable web security)
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer html \
  --web-browser-flag="--disable-web-security" \
  --web-browser-flag="--allow-running-insecure-content"
```

### Code Generation & Dependencies

#### Code Generation (JSON, Freezed, etc.)
```bash
# 🔨 Generate code once
flutter packages pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs

# 👀 Watch mode (continuous generation)
flutter packages pub run build_runner watch --delete-conflicting-outputs

# 🧹 Clean generated files
flutter packages pub run build_runner clean
```

#### Dependencies Management
```bash
# 📦 Get dependencies
flutter pub get

# 🔄 Upgrade dependencies
flutter pub upgrade

# 🧹 Clean project
flutter clean && flutter pub get
```

### Building for Production

#### Standard Build
```bash
# 🏗️ Optimized web build
flutter build web --web-renderer html --release

# 📦 Build with environment
flutter build web --web-renderer html --release \
  --dart-define=ENV=production \
  --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=https://api.plattr.pro
```

#### Testing Built App Locally
```bash
# 🌐 Serve built app for testing
python3 -m http.server 8000 -d build/web

# 🔍 Alternative with Node.js
npx http-server build/web -p 8000 -c-1
```

### Logging & Debugging

#### Log Filtering (using existing script)
```bash
# 📝 Cart-specific logs
./run_with_logs.sh && grep -E '(CART|💰|🛒)' logs/flutter_run.log

# 🔍 API logs
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --debug | grep -E '(API|HTTP|RESPONSE)'

# ❌ Error logs only
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --debug | grep -E '(ERROR|EXCEPTION|FAILED)'
```

### Troubleshooting

#### Common Issues
```bash
# 🔄 Complete reset
flutter clean && rm -rf .dart_tool && rm -f pubspec.lock && flutter pub get

# 🏥 Flutter doctor check
flutter doctor -v

# 📱 List available devices
flutter devices

# 🔧 Fix pub cache issues
flutter pub cache repair
```

#### Hot Reload Issues
- If hot reload stops: Press `R` for hot restart
- Clear browser cache: `Cmd+Shift+R` (Mac) or `Ctrl+Shift+R` (Windows/Linux)
- Check terminal for compilation errors
- Ensure port 8080 is not used by other processes

#### Performance Issues
```bash
# 🐌 Slow build debugging
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer html \
  --verbose --trace-startup

# 💾 Memory issues
flutter run -d chrome --web-port 8080 --web-renderer html \
  --profile --dart-vm-options="--old-gen-heap-size=4096"
```

